---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';

const repo = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_REPO_URL || 'https://github.com/hk-vk/badgebar';
---

<Legal
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="BadgeBar collects nothing. It runs entirely on your Mac and never connects to the internet."
  updated="October 20, 2026"
>
  <p>
    BadgeBar collects nothing about you. It runs entirely on your Mac, has no account, and never
    connects to the internet. There are no analytics, no crash reports and no servers.
  </p>

  <h2>What the app reads</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Badges on the Dock.</strong> With Accessibility permission, BadgeBar reads the unread
      counts macOS shows on Dock icons, so it can show them in the menu bar.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Notification history, if you allow it.</strong> With Full Disk Access, BadgeBar reads
      the notifications macOS has already saved on your Mac, to show recent messages when you
      right-click an icon. This is optional. Without it, you still get the counts.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>Both are read on your Mac, used only to draw the menu bar, and never sent anywhere.</p>

  <h2>What the app stores</h2>
  <p>BadgeBar keeps a small amount of data on your Mac, in your user account:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Your settings, which apps you added, and what you marked as read, in
      <code>~/Library/Preferences/io.github.hk-vk.badgebar.plist</code>.
    </li>
    <li>
      Copies of images you choose as icons, in
      <code>~/Library/Application Support/BadgeBar/</code>.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    To remove all of it, quit BadgeBar and delete those two locations, or run
    <code>brew uninstall --zap --cask badgebar</code> if you installed it with Homebrew.
  </p>

  <h2>This website</h2>
  <p>
    This site has no cookies, analytics or trackers. If you pick Light or Dark in the footer, the
    choice is saved in your browser and never leaves it. The site is hosted on GitHub Pages, and
    downloads come from GitHub Releases, so GitHub may log technical details like your IP address
    as described in the <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub Privacy Statement</a>.
    Homebrew has its own <a href="https://docs.brew.sh/Analytics">analytics policy</a> for installs made through it.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If BadgeBar ever starts handling data differently, this page will change first, and the date at
    the top will show when.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about privacy are welcome as an <a href={`${repo}/issues`}>issue on GitHub</a>.
  </p>
</Legal>
